  "id": "Compound::DB00496 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Darifenacin, a cholinergic muscarinic antagonist, is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Darifenacin may influence Cyp3a4 via indirect pathways, as it is associated with Acute Retention of Urine, which is linked to Meloxicam and Disopyramide, both of which bind to Cyp3a4. This indicates that Darifenacin may modulate Cyp3a4 activity through the pharmacological effects of these compounds, potentially altering metabolic processes involving Cyp3a4. The presence of a common ancestor in the Organic Molecule category further supports a shared biological role in the pathway. The mechanism appears to involve the interaction of Darifenacin with other agents that affect the nervous system or are organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds, which may indirectly influence Cyp3a4. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Darifenacin in modulating Cyp3a4 activity through a complex network of pharmacological and biochemical interactions.",
